00:09:58.959 --> 00:10:02.709
Especially in the short, hard-hitting, seasonal anime culture. as they can

00:10:02.709 --> 00:10:05.540
Sometimes feel like certain anime were made as a glorified

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.700
advert for the source material

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:12.380
see, when it comes to people who read source material like manga there are two types of manga readers:

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:17.500
the brain, rare heroic Souls who throw themselves into the Expansive world of manga

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:23.800
working tirelessly to find that next hidden gem within the ocean of unknown titles

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:28.920
and then, there's everyone else, who saw an airing anime and couldn't wait to find out what happens next.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.240
back in the day there were some pretty infamous endings for doing this and by infamous

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.350
I mean it was like the animators ran out of paper to draw on and we're like, yeah

