00:11:59.899 --> 00:12:05.198
Not likely. part of the life cycle within the anime and manga culture is that we get an anime adaptation

00:12:05.389 --> 00:12:08.529
When you have a hot title and that rarely happens

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:12.939
After a title has already ended. On the rare occasion you get something like Devil man Crybaby

00:12:12.949 --> 00:12:15.789
where the anime is adapting an old title that's finished

00:12:15.789 --> 00:12:20.560
But more often than not you find yourself finishing the anime and when you catch up to the manga or light novel,

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.860
the story is still at least a few years away from completion

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:30.160
one thing I both love and hate about the medium of anime is just how many new shows with massive variety we constantly get

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.660
but the downside of that, is as an anime fan you get used to being introduced to stories, characters, and worlds

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:39.100
which you know you're never gonna see the ending of and honestly

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:44.170
I think that's kind of a shame because to me even though I don't think the ending is always the most

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:51.339
Important factor a lot of the anime that have stuck in my mind. years after they have finished. are the ones that end.

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:01.400
Now you may be sitting there wondering why I cared enough about

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:04.190
Anime endings that I would want to make a whole video on it

