00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:51.580
I remember season 2, episode 25, Re;

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:54.349
I remember Lelouch's sacrifice

00:13:54.710 --> 00:13:56.960
I remember the Trumpets of Madder Sky

00:13:57.270 --> 00:14:03.949
Blaring as they explained Zero's Requiem. jaws wide open, goosebumps galore. as I realized

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:07.159
Holy fuck. everything had a point

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:12.469
Everything was leading up to this one moment and feeling a sense of awe

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:19.700
jubilation, sadness, and emptiness. all at once as the credits started rolling and

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:23.449
That is the power of a great ending

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:27.780
It's that bittersweet void that tells you that the journey is Over

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:33.160
as much as you love the path you took to get here and never wanted it to end

00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:37.130
The fact that it did end makes it even more special

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:44.420
And you wouldn't have it any other way. Because yes, sometimes it's about the journey, not the destination

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:47.460
but when you have a breathtaking destination,

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:50.660
it can give even more meaning to that journey,

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:56.040
and make that entire voyage you took THAT much more extraordinary

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:59.660
Nowadays so much focus is given to how to begin a story.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:02.760
With so many anime competing
for your attention every season,

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:06.180
it's all about how to make
the highest impact as fast as possible,

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:08.640
how to immediately stand out from the crowd.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:12.200
But to me, it's the ending that sticks with you.

00:15:12.209 --> 00:15:17.249
There have been plenty of anime with great beginnings that slowly fizzle out and get forgotten

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:22.259
But I have never forgotten an anime with a great ending

00:15:22.269 --> 00:15:25.169
It wraps up everything the story was trying to say

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:28.400
Allows me to truly reflect on the anime as a whole

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:32.100
and kind of make peace with the fact that it is complete.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.640
Because, if you end your anime right,

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:39.940
